\DOC ASSEMBLER_SIMPLIFY_TAC

\TYPE {ASSEMBLER_SIMPLIFY_TAC : tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Simplifies the conclusion of the goal in place, rewriting with the assumptions
and evaluating arithmetic/word subterms, leaving the assumption list untouched.

\DESCRIBE
Takes no arguments.
{
   A ?- t
   =========================  ASSEMBLER_SIMPLIFY_TAC
   A ?- u
}
\noindent Here {u} is {t} with subterms simplified: component reads mentioned
in {A} are replaced by the values those assumptions give them, nested address
and offset arithmetic is folded, numeric literals are normalised, boolean
equivalences with a constant truth value are collapsed into plain or negated
atoms, and other arithmetic/word subexpressions are reduced. No assumption is
added or removed.

\COMMENTS
In all observed traces the conclusion was an implication whose antecedent
(describing one machine step) is what gets simplified, while the rest of the
conclusion is largely unchanged; no trace shows the goal being closed or split.

\ENDDOC
